From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan Murray <ryan@aurorasilicon.org>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 14:04:34 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: soc: apple: apple,t6041-aop: Add memory-region

The AOP firmware runs its external code and its log from DRAM. Describe
those segments as memory-region entries, which the bootloader fills in
from the ADT, with the address the firmware uses for each one in the
region's iommu-addresses, as for the other Apple coprocessors whose
firmware the bootloader loads.

This replaces the aop-etext and aop-oslog reserved-memory nodes that the
description named, which no binding defined and nothing referred to.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Ryan Murray <ryan@aurorasilicon.org>
(cherry picked from commit 79de87a95447539276c318a6ac9bf230e3a659a5)
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
---
 .../bindings/soc/apple/apple,t6041-aop.yaml       | 15 +++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/soc/apple/apple,t6041-aop.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/soc/apple/apple,t6041-aop.yaml
index d81cde8a8d..e8a2df8050 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/soc/apple/apple,t6041-aop.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/soc/apple/apple,t6041-aop.yaml
@@ -13,10 +13,8 @@ description:
   The Always-On Processor provides audio and sensor services through firmware
   loaded by the bootloader. The application processor patches the firmware's
   boot arguments in the AOP SRAM, starts it through RTKit over one mailbox and
-  reaches its services through the RTKit endpoints. The bootloader reserves
-  the firmware's external code and log segments as /reserved-memory nodes
-  named aop-etext and aop-oslog; no mapping of them survives the reset of the
-  AOP's DART, so the operating system maps them again before the start.
+  reaches its services through the RTKit endpoints. The firmware's external
+  code and log segments live in DRAM, and the bootloader reserves them.
 
 properties:
   compatible:
@@ -47,6 +45,14 @@ properties:
   iommus:
     maxItems: 1
 
+  memory-region:
+    minItems: 1
+    maxItems: 4
+    description:
+      The firmware segments in DRAM (its external code and its log), filled in
+      by the bootloader from the ADT. The iommu-addresses property of each
+      region gives the address the firmware uses for it.
+
   audio:
     type: object
     $ref: /schemas/sound/apple,t6041-aop-audio.yaml#
@@ -105,6 +111,7 @@ examples:
             mboxes = <&aop_mbox>;
             mbox-names = "mbox";
             iommus = <&aop_dart 0>;
+            memory-region = <&aop_etext>, <&aop_oslog>; /* Filled by the bootloader */
 
             als {
                 compatible = "apple,t6041-aop-als", "apple,aop-als";
